  "summary": "The study wet-spun Ti3C2Tx MXene/PEDOT:PSS hybrid fibers from LiF/HCl MILD-delaminated MXene using a 98 wt. % H2SO4 coagulation bath. Five explicitly reported fiber electrodes were identified: the neat PEDOT:PSS control and M1P9, M3P7, M5P5, and M7P3 hybrid compositions. M7P3, containing approximately 70 wt. % MXene, was the headline electrode and delivered 614.5 F cm-3 at 5 mV s-1 in 1 M H2SO4 using a three-electrode setup. The manuscript does not state electrode mass loading, thickness, BET area, porosity, pore size, tortuosity, or numerical gravimetric capacitances for these individual fibers."
}